{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 42, :comments ["<b>A night of watchfulness it is to YHWH, to bring them out.</b> For He was waiting to bring them out, for He did not afflict them willingly; but He did not find Israel prepared and worthy of redemption until that night. And that night He was watching and waiting, for He desires kindness, as the Sages of blessed memory said: the Holy One, blessed be He, calculates the end." "<b>This same night is a night of watchfulness to YHWH.</b> Just as He watched and waited for Israel's redemption all the days of their exile in Egypt, so He watches and waits for Israel's future redemption, as it says: וְלָכֵן יְחַכֶּה ה' לַחֲנַנְכֶם (Isaiah 30:18)." "<b>For all the children of Israel throughout their generations.</b> As the Sages said (Rosh HaShanah 11a): בְּנִיסָן נִגְאֲלוּ, וּבְנִיסָן עֲתִידִין לְהִגָּאֵל."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:25:19.599779597Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}